  "timeoriginalestimate": null,
  "description": {
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1,
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "1. What happens now",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "When a Technician Utilization download starts, the message reads \"Success / Data exported successfully.\" When a download fails, no message appears at all - the user is simply left with no file and no explanation."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "2. What should happen instead",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Technician Utilization specification, version 6, Story 7 error handling and the section 7 notifications table close both wordings: a download that starts shows \"Download started\", and a download that fails shows \"Failed to download report\"."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "3. How to see it",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Open Reports > Technician Utilization and set the date range to This Quarter. Open the three-dot menu, choose Summary (CSV), and read the message that appears."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Then set the date range to This Year and choose Expanded (PDF). Wait about forty seconds and watch for any message."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Exact test data this was seen with: organisation Staging Foothills Group Inc; signed-in user Admin ShopView; active location Staging Heavy Duty - 9919; the other accessible location Staging Lethbridge - 4310; date range This Year (1 January 2026 to 6 August 2026), which returns 29 technicians."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "4. What was actually shown",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The successful download showed \"Success / Data exported successfully.\" - the same generic wording for all four options, naming neither the report nor the file type."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The failed download showed nothing. The server answered the request with an error after roughly half a minute, no file arrived, and no message of any kind was displayed."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "5. What was ruled out",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "It is not a message that appeared and vanished before it could be read. The screen was checked continuously for forty-five seconds after the failure and no notification was ever present."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "It is not the download quietly succeeding. No file was produced."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Note for triage: the underlying reason that Expanded PDF fails on a large view is already reported as SV-8818, which names this report. This ticket is only about the missing and generic messages."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Note for triage: the same generic success wording was reported on Parts Velocity as SV-8936. This ticket is the Technician Utilization report, which has its own written wordings."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "6. How often",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Every time, for both the success and the failure message."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "7. Where it was seen",
       "marks": [
        {
         "type": "strong"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Reports > Technician Utilization, on the QA branch, build v3.5-16cf83f, on 6 August 2026."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": " "
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "Where this expected behaviour comes from: the Technician Utilization report specification, version 6, Story 7 under Error Handling, which gives both wordings: \"When a download starts, the user sees a success notification: \u201cDownload started\u201d.\" and \"If a download fails, the user sees an error notification: \u201cFailed to download report\u201d.\""
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The same two appear again in the notifications table in section 7 of that specification, where the trigger \"A download starts\" is paired with the message \"Download started\", and the trigger \"A download fails\" with the message \"Failed to download report\"."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
